1
00:00:11,924 --> 00:00:15,232
[indistinct conversations]

2
00:00:22,239 --> 00:00:23,588
[beeps]

3
00:00:23,588 --> 00:00:25,068
[door unlocks]

4
00:00:38,255 --> 00:00:40,170
[computer whirring]

5
00:00:40,170 --> 00:00:41,389
[beeps]

6
00:00:41,389 --> 00:00:44,044
[door whooshing]

7
00:00:51,181 --> 00:00:53,444
[air hisses]

8
00:01:00,103 --> 00:01:03,976
[clicks]

9
00:01:30,177 --> 00:01:33,136
[man] I DARESAY YOU'VE INSPECTED
MORE MODERN FACILITIES

10
00:01:33,136 --> 00:01:35,138
IN YOUR TRAVELS, BUT, UH--

11
00:01:35,138 --> 00:01:38,881
GRIFFIN.
DON'T COME IN HERE.

12
00:01:38,881 --> 00:01:40,317
DR. SEBERG, WHAT'S WRONG?

13
00:01:45,235 --> 00:01:47,107
OH, MY GOD.

14
00:01:55,158 --> 00:01:58,030
[shoes shuffling]

15
00:02:01,251 --> 00:02:03,035
[shuffles]

16
00:02:04,341 --> 00:02:06,735
HEY.

17
00:02:06,735 --> 00:02:08,432
HEY.

18
00:02:08,432 --> 00:02:10,913
CHEER UP.WHY?

19
00:02:10,913 --> 00:02:13,045
UH, 'CAUSE IT'S BETTER
TO BE HAPPY THAN SAD.

20
00:02:13,045 --> 00:02:15,831
I'M NOT SAD.YOU'RE VERY SAD.

21
00:02:15,831 --> 00:02:19,487
YOU'VE BEEN SAD FOR MONTHS,
EVER SINCE, UH--WHAT, IS THIS SOME SORT
OF THERAPY SESSION?

22
00:02:19,487 --> 00:02:22,098
DID YOU BRING TISSUE
IN CASE YOU MAKE ME CRY?

23
00:02:22,098 --> 00:02:24,666
THERE WE GO. ZING OF ANGER--
GETS THE BLOOD UP.

24
00:02:24,666 --> 00:02:27,712
THAT'S A GOOD START.IS THIS WHAT YOU CAME HERE FOR--
TO ZING ME?

25
00:02:27,712 --> 00:02:31,151
BECAUSE I'VE GOT
PAPERWORK TO DO.JANE, CALL FOR YOU. THEY SAY
IT'S EXTREMELY URGENT. LINE TWO.

26
00:02:31,151 --> 00:02:33,457
OOH.

27
00:02:33,457 --> 00:02:35,067
[picks up telephone receiver]

28
00:02:35,067 --> 00:02:37,157
[clears throat]
THIS IS JANE.

29
00:02:37,157 --> 00:02:39,159
[woman] Good morning, Mr. Jane.

30
00:02:39,159 --> 00:02:42,118
MY NAME IS DR. ALICIA SEBERG.

31
00:02:42,118 --> 00:02:44,512
I GATHER FROM A BRIEF SEARCH
ON THE INTERNET

32
00:02:44,512 --> 00:02:46,601
THAT YOU'RE THE BEST DETECTIVE
IN MY IMMEDIATE VICINITY.

33
00:02:46,601 --> 00:02:48,429
OH. WELL, UM...

34
00:02:48,429 --> 00:02:52,302
YOU FLATTER ME, BUT, UH,
I'M NOT ACTUALLY A DETECTIVE.

35
00:02:52,302 --> 00:02:53,651
I NEED
YOUR PROFESSIONAL ASSISTANCE.

36
00:02:53,651 --> 00:02:55,175
Please come immediately.

37
00:02:55,175 --> 00:02:56,828
I'VE BEEN MURDERED.

38
00:03:07,926 --> 00:03:10,886
[helicopter whirring]

39
00:03:34,953 --> 00:03:36,520
WHOO!

40
00:03:38,827 --> 00:03:41,656
THAT WAS FUN!

41
00:03:41,656 --> 00:03:43,397
[Patrick] WHOO!

42
00:03:43,397 --> 00:03:47,444
AGENT LISBON! CBI!

43
00:03:47,444 --> 00:03:49,664
MA'AM, SIR,
PLEASE FOLLOW ME.

44
00:03:49,664 --> 00:03:50,882
ALL RIGHT!

45
00:03:50,882 --> 00:03:53,842
AGENT LISBON.
AND YOU ARE...

46
00:03:53,842 --> 00:03:55,757
I'M THIS GUY--
PATRICK JANE. CONSULTANT?

47
00:03:55,757 --> 00:03:58,673
OKAY, TERESA, PATRICK,
GLAD TO MEET YOU BOTH.

48
00:03:58,673 --> 00:04:01,284
I'M DEAN HARKEN, CALIFORNIA
DISEASE CONTROL AUTHORITY.

49
00:04:01,284 --> 00:04:03,591
NICE TO MEET YOU.YEAH, WE HAVE

50
00:04:03,591 --> 00:04:05,941
A POTENTIAL CODE RED
VIRUS OUTBREAK SITUATION HERE.

51
00:04:05,941 --> 00:04:08,726
THIS FACILITY
IS UNDER C.D.C.A. CONTROL,

52
00:04:08,726 --> 00:04:10,859
AS PER
STATE EMERGENCY PROTOCOLS.

53
00:04:10,859 --> 00:04:13,818
THOUSANDS OF PEOPLE MIGHT DIE IF
WE DON'T GET THIS RIGHT, OKAY?

54
00:04:13,818 --> 00:04:16,778
WE'VE BEEN APPRISED
OF THE BASIC--NOW SHE'S DENYING IT, OF COURSE,
BUT THIS SITUATION'S

55
00:04:16,778 --> 00:04:18,432
ALMOST CERTAINLY RESULTED
FROM AN ERROR BY DR. SEBERG.

56
00:04:18,432 --> 00:04:20,912
THERE'S NO CRIMINALITY
INVOLVED,

57
00:04:20,912 --> 00:04:23,915
SO YOU'RE NOT REALLY
NEEDED HERE.PROBABLY,
BUT WE'RE GONNA HAVE--

58
00:04:23,915 --> 00:04:26,701
AS A PROFESSIONAL COURTESY, I'M
GONNA LET YOU INTO THE FACILITY.

59
00:04:26,701 --> 00:04:29,181
I'M HAPPY FOR YOU GUYS
TO OBSERVE AND GATHER EVIDENCE,

60
00:04:29,181 --> 00:04:32,184
AS LONG AS YOU REMEMBER
THAT C.D.C.A. IS BIG DOG HERE.

61
00:04:32,184 --> 00:04:35,187
OUR INVESTIGATION HAS PRIORITY.
NOW ARE WE COOL WITH THAT?

62
00:04:35,187 --> 00:04:36,319
ABSOLUTELY.

63
00:04:36,319 --> 00:04:38,539
CAN I SEE
YOUR I.D. ALSO?

64
00:04:38,539 --> 00:04:40,628
SURE.

65
00:04:42,282 --> 00:04:45,937
THANK YOU... DEAN.

66
00:04:45,937 --> 00:04:49,724
NO PICTURE. THAT'S A SHAME.
YOU'RE A GOOD-LOOKING MAN.

67
00:04:49,724 --> 00:04:52,204
SCOTT PRICE,
I MANAGE THIS FACILITY

68
00:04:52,204 --> 00:04:53,815
FOR ZITEK
BIOSYSTEMS DIVISION.

69
00:04:53,815 --> 00:04:55,512
RIGHT OFF THE BAT,
LET ME ASSURE YOU

70
00:04:55,512 --> 00:04:58,907
THAT WE AS A COMPANY ARE
110% COMMITTED TO GIVING YOU

71
00:04:58,907 --> 00:05:02,389
THE BEST POSSIBLE COOPERATION.THANK YOU, MR. PRICE. SHALL WE?
THERE'S A SENSE OF URGENCY HERE.

72
00:05:02,389 --> 00:05:05,696
AH, YES, OF COURSE.

73
00:05:05,696 --> 00:05:08,046
LISBON, JANE, DR. EDMUNDS,
HEAD OF RESEARCH HERE.

74
00:05:08,046 --> 00:05:10,048
HE'LL TAKE YOU
TO THE RELEASE INCIDENT.

75
00:05:10,048 --> 00:05:12,790
PRICE, COME WITH ME.

76
00:05:12,790 --> 00:05:14,792
THANK YOU FOR COMING
SO QUICKLY.

77
00:05:14,792 --> 00:05:17,186
WHAT EXACTLY IS IT
THAT YOU DO HERE?

78
00:05:17,186 --> 00:05:18,796
BIOWARFARE.
WITH MODERN TECHNOLOGY,

79
00:05:18,796 --> 00:05:21,321
ANTHRAX, BOTULISM,
BUBONIC PLAGUE,

80
00:05:21,321 --> 00:05:24,106
EVEN COBRA VENOM ALL HAVE
STRONG WEAPONIZING POTENTIAL.

81
00:05:24,106 --> 00:05:26,761
IT'S A GROWING FIELD.
A LOT OF EXCITING DEVELOPMENTS.

82
00:05:26,761 --> 00:05:29,329
YOU DEVELOP WAYS OF KILLING
PEOPLE IN LARGE NUMBERS.

83
00:05:29,329 --> 00:05:31,722
TO THE CONTRARY. WE DEVELOP
ANTIDOTES, WAYS TO COMBAT

84
00:05:31,722 --> 00:05:33,855
THE THINGS THAT KILL
LARGE NUMBERS OF PEOPLE.

85
00:05:33,855 --> 00:05:35,465
HERE WE ARE.

86
00:05:35,465 --> 00:05:39,817
[computer whirring]

87
00:05:39,817 --> 00:05:41,210
[beeps]

88
00:05:41,210 --> 00:05:42,690
[door unlocks]FOLLOW ME.

89
00:05:45,606 --> 00:05:48,086
120.

90
00:05:48,086 --> 00:05:51,568
DARLING. IS THIS MR. JANE?

91
00:05:51,568 --> 00:05:54,397
YES. HOW ARE YOU FEELING?THE SAME.

92
00:05:54,397 --> 00:05:56,399
INTERESTING IMPROVEMENT
IN CARDIAC RATE, THOUGH.

93
00:05:56,399 --> 00:06:00,055
MY METABOLISM'S TRYING TO
FIGHT BACK WITH ADRENALINE.

94
00:06:00,055 --> 00:06:02,100
GOOD MORNING, MR. JANE.

95
00:06:02,100 --> 00:06:03,972
HI.

96
00:06:03,972 --> 00:06:05,756
AGENT LISBON, CBI.

97
00:06:07,497 --> 00:06:09,891
YOU MIND WRITING THIS DOWN
FOR US?

98
00:06:09,891 --> 00:06:13,851
SOMEONE OPENED THIS FLASK
AND LEFT IT UNDER THE TANK.

99
00:06:13,851 --> 00:06:17,072
IT CONTAINS AN AIRBORNE FORM
OF CRYPTOHANSA B STRAIN.

100
00:06:17,072 --> 00:06:19,379
IT'S
AN ENGINEERED SUPERVIRUS.

101
00:06:19,379 --> 00:06:22,120
IF IT ESCAPED FROM THIS ROOM,
IT WOULD KILL

102
00:06:22,120 --> 00:06:24,558
EVERY VERTEBRATE CREATURE
WITHIN A QUARTER-MILE RADIUS.

103
00:06:24,558 --> 00:06:27,648
IT ATTACKS THE RED BLOOD CELLS,
GRADUALLY STOPS THEM

104
00:06:27,648 --> 00:06:29,693
FROM DELIVERING OXYGEN.

105
00:06:29,693 --> 00:06:31,956
THE VICTIM... DIES FROM
SUFFOCATION OR A HEART ATTACK,

106
00:06:31,956 --> 00:06:34,089
DEPENDING ON
THEIR PHYSICAL CONDITION.

107
00:06:34,089 --> 00:06:35,873
HOW LONG AFTER EXPOSURE?

108
00:06:35,873 --> 00:06:38,615
WE ESTIMATE ANYWHERE
FROM TWO TO SIX HOURS.

109
00:06:38,615 --> 00:06:42,750
SO YOU COULD DIE AT ANY TIME?YES.

110
00:06:42,750 --> 00:06:45,361
HARKEN SAYS YOU DID THIS
YOURSELF--TRAGIC ERROR.

111
00:06:45,361 --> 00:06:48,364
HE'S A BUREAUCRAT. HE'S LOOKING
FOR THE EASY ANSWER.

112
00:06:48,364 --> 00:06:50,845
IT TAKES FOUR DISTINCT STEPS
TO REMOVE A CAP

113
00:06:50,845 --> 00:06:53,804
FROM ONE OF THESE FLASKS,
AND WE NEVER OPEN A FLASK

114
00:06:53,804 --> 00:06:56,154
OUTSIDE OF THE TANK.
THAT'S JUST BASIC.

115
00:06:56,154 --> 00:07:00,028
I CAN ASSURE YOU BOTH,
I HAD NOTHING TO DO WITH THIS.

116
00:07:00,028 --> 00:07:03,335
BUT THIS WAS NO MISTAKE.
WHOEVER DID THIS WANTED ME DEAD.

117
00:07:03,335 --> 00:07:05,642
EVERYBODY KNOWS I TAKE
THE FIRST SHIFT.

118
00:07:05,642 --> 00:07:08,906
SHE CALLED YOU "DARLING."
YOU BOTH HAVE WEDDING BANDS.

119
00:07:08,906 --> 00:07:10,778
YOU HUSBAND AND WIFE?

120
00:07:10,778 --> 00:07:12,519
YES.

121
00:07:14,172 --> 00:07:15,957
WELL, SHE LOOKS SURPRISED

122
00:07:15,957 --> 00:07:18,786
BECAUSE YOU SEEM
INCREDIBLY CALM AND COOL

123
00:07:18,786 --> 00:07:20,657
FOR A MAN WHOSE WIFE
IS DYING.

124
00:07:20,657 --> 00:07:24,139
HOW WOULD AN ABSENCE OF CALM
AND COOL BE USEFUL TO HER?

125
00:07:24,139 --> 00:07:26,271
GOOD POINT.
CORRECT ME IF I'M WRONG,

126
00:07:26,271 --> 00:07:28,448
BUT FOR THE KILLER TO OPEN
THE FLASK,

127
00:07:28,448 --> 00:07:30,798
THEY WOULD HAVE TO EXPOSE
THEMSELVES TO THE VIRUS,

128
00:07:30,798 --> 00:07:34,149
IN WHICH CASE, THEY WOULD BE
DYING OR POSSIBLY DEAD ALREADY.

129
00:07:34,149 --> 00:07:36,630
NO, THERE'S AN ANTIDOTE.

130
00:07:36,630 --> 00:07:38,675
IT'S AN ENZYME COMPOUND.

131
00:07:38,675 --> 00:07:41,635
IF TAKEN BEFORE EXPOSURE,
IT PREVENTS INFECTION.

132
00:07:41,635 --> 00:07:43,985
I ASSUME WHOEVER DID THIS
TOOK A DOSE.

133
00:07:43,985 --> 00:07:47,336
COULDN'T YOU J--NO, I CAN'T TAKE IT NOW.

134
00:07:47,336 --> 00:07:51,209
THE ANTIDOTE ONLY WORKS IF TAKEN
BEFOREEXPOSURE, AS I SAID.

135
00:07:51,209 --> 00:07:53,951
WHY DIDN'T YOU TAKE IT BEFORE,
JUST AS A PRECAUTION?

136
00:07:53,951 --> 00:07:57,128
THE SIDE EFFECTS OF REGULAR USE
ARE FAR TOO SEVERE.

137
00:07:57,128 --> 00:07:59,217
WHO ELSE HAD ACCESS
TO THE VIRUS FLASK?

138
00:07:59,217 --> 00:08:01,698
THE ONLY PEOPLE ALLOWED
IN THE LAB ARE CLIFF AND I,

139
00:08:01,698 --> 00:08:04,135
WELKS, NASH AND TRIPP,
OUR COLLEAGUES.

140
00:08:04,135 --> 00:08:06,616
WE HAVE A STATE-OF-THE-ART
BIOMETRIC SECURITY SYSTEM,

141
00:08:06,616 --> 00:08:08,096
AS YOU CAN SEE.

142
00:08:08,096 --> 00:08:11,055
SO YOUR HUSBAND
OR ONE OF THE THREE COLLEAGUES

143
00:08:11,055 --> 00:08:12,883
IS THE KILLER.

144
00:08:14,319 --> 00:08:17,497
SORRY. UH, WILLBE THE KILLER.

145
00:08:17,497 --> 00:08:19,281
JANE.

146
00:08:19,281 --> 00:08:20,412
I'M JUST... MM.

147
00:08:22,240 --> 00:08:25,374
THAT'S ALL RIGHT. THAT IS
THE UNAVOIDABLE CONCLUSION.

148
00:08:25,374 --> 00:08:27,028
YES.

149
00:08:27,028 --> 00:08:29,596
WHERE ARE
THE OTHER THREE NOW?

150
00:08:29,596 --> 00:08:33,034
HARKEN IS HAVING THEM
FILL OUT AN ACCIDENT REPORT.WE'RE GONNA NEED TO SPEAK
TO THEM.

151
00:08:33,034 --> 00:08:35,471
OOH, THIS IS
A GOOD ONE, EH?

152
00:08:35,471 --> 00:08:37,299
GOOD?

153
00:08:37,299 --> 00:08:39,562
WELL, INTERESTING. UNIQUE.

154
00:08:39,562 --> 00:08:43,566
IF YOU'RE A JADED, GHOULISH
ADVENTURE SEEKER.

155
00:08:43,566 --> 00:08:45,960
GHOULISH? LISTEN, IF PEOPLE
ARE GONNA KILL EACH OTHER

156
00:08:45,960 --> 00:08:48,571
AND WE HAVE TO CATCH THEM,
I WOULD MUCH RATHER

157
00:08:48,571 --> 00:08:50,921
THEY GO ABOUT IT WITH
SOME KIND OF ORIGINALITY.

158
00:08:50,921 --> 00:08:52,749
[Van Pelt] Boss?HEY, VAN PELT.

159
00:08:52,749 --> 00:08:55,143
I need you to do background
checks on Cliff Edmunds...

160
00:08:55,143 --> 00:08:58,102
[speaking indistinctly]LILITH NASH,
GRIFFIN LATIMER WELKS,

161
00:08:58,102 --> 00:08:59,800
Florian Eric Tripp.

162
00:08:59,800 --> 00:09:01,497
I'm sending you
their details now.

163
00:09:01,497 --> 00:09:04,500
ANYTHING TO BE
LOOKING OUT FOR IN PARTICULAR?

164
00:09:04,500 --> 00:09:06,763
OH, UH, ONE OF THEM RELEASED
A LETHAL SUPERVIRUS

165
00:09:06,763 --> 00:09:08,504
THAT COULD KILL HALF
THE STATE OF CALIFORNIA,

166
00:09:08,504 --> 00:09:10,201
so I guess we're looking for

167
00:09:10,201 --> 00:09:12,900
someone with a prior background
as an evil supervillain.

168
00:09:12,900 --> 00:09:14,292
OKAY.

169
00:09:16,599 --> 00:09:19,689
THAT LAST PART WAS A JOKE.YEAH, WE GET IT.

170
00:09:19,689 --> 00:09:20,951
Later.

171
00:09:30,482 --> 00:09:32,006
HELLO.

172
00:09:32,006 --> 00:09:33,224
HI.

173
00:09:33,224 --> 00:09:34,530
HELLO.HELLO.

174
00:09:38,403 --> 00:09:40,580
[clears throat]

175
00:09:42,190 --> 00:09:44,975
[sighs deeply]

176
00:09:44,975 --> 00:09:48,196
WHAT ARE YOU DOIN'?WHAT DOES IT LOOK LIKE
I'M DOING?

177
00:09:48,196 --> 00:09:52,722
TRYING TO MAKE US NERVOUS?CORRECT. HOW AM I DOING?

178
00:09:52,722 --> 00:09:55,116
DOING WELL.EXCELLENT.

179
00:09:55,116 --> 00:09:57,292
BUT WHY?

180
00:09:57,292 --> 00:10:00,034
ONE OF YOU THREE
MURDERED ALICIA SEBERG,

181
00:10:00,034 --> 00:10:04,038
OR HER HUSBAND DID.
IT'S OUR JOB TO FIND OUT WHO.AND WE'RE IN A HURRY,

182
00:10:04,038 --> 00:10:08,129
AND NERVOUS PEOPLE
ARE EASY TO READ.AND WHAT DO YOU GATHER
FROM ALL THIS READING?

183
00:10:08,129 --> 00:10:10,218
WELL, YOU'RE AN OPEN BOOK.
YOU'RE EXACTLY WHAT

184
00:10:10,218 --> 00:10:12,742
YOU SEEM TO BE--
A STRAIGHT ARROW, A BOY SCOUT.

185
00:10:12,742 --> 00:10:15,527
AM I RIGHT?NO.

186
00:10:15,527 --> 00:10:18,400
I'M WRONG.
THERE'S A HIDDEN SIDE TO YOU.YES, BUT--

187
00:10:18,400 --> 00:10:20,532
WHAT ARE YOU HIDING?NOTHING.

188
00:10:20,532 --> 00:10:22,665
WHAT IS HE HIDING, LILITH?I DON'T KNOW.

189
00:10:22,665 --> 00:10:24,232
WHAT ARE YOUHIDING?I-I'M NOT--

190
00:10:24,232 --> 00:10:25,799
IT WAS YOU, WASN'T IT?ME WHAT?

191
00:10:25,799 --> 00:10:28,715
YOU WERE HAVING AN AFFAIR
WITH ALICIA SEBERG.

192
00:10:28,715 --> 00:10:30,934
WHAT? NO, NOT WITH ME.

193
00:10:30,934 --> 00:10:34,764
NOT WITH YOU.
WITH WHO, THEN?

194
00:10:34,764 --> 00:10:36,766
I OVERSEE EQUIPMENT
AND INVENTORY,

195
00:10:36,766 --> 00:10:38,899
NOT MY COLLEAGUES'
PRIVATE LIVES.

196
00:10:38,899 --> 00:10:40,770
BUT SHE WASHAVING
AN AFFAIR, HUH?

197
00:10:40,770 --> 00:10:43,773
WHY ELSE WOULD A HUSBAND
HAVE THE MOTIVES TO KILL HER?

198
00:10:43,773 --> 00:10:46,733
AND IF IT WASN'T HER HUSBAND,
IT WAS ONE OF YOU.

199
00:10:46,733 --> 00:10:48,256
WHO WAS IT?

200
00:10:51,868 --> 00:10:53,565
MY GUESS...

201
00:10:55,655 --> 00:10:57,613
KASEEM.[knocks on table]

202
00:10:57,613 --> 00:10:59,702
YES.

203
00:10:59,702 --> 00:11:01,486
DOES HER HUSBAND KNOW?OH, HE KNOWS.

204
00:11:01,486 --> 00:11:03,097
DR. EDMUNDS IS

205
00:11:03,097 --> 00:11:05,665
A KIND, GENTLE MAN.
HE COULDN'T HAVE DONE THIS.

206
00:11:05,665 --> 00:11:08,319
THANK YOU, LILITH, FLORIAN...

207
00:11:08,319 --> 00:11:09,756
GRIFFIN.

208
00:11:19,069 --> 00:11:22,377
WHY DIDN'T YOU TELL US YOU WERE
HAVING AN AFFAIR

209
00:11:22,377 --> 00:11:25,075
WITH DR. KASEEM HERE?BECAUSE IT ISN'T RELEVANT.

210
00:11:25,075 --> 00:11:27,643
YEAH, WE HAVE
AN HONEST AND OPEN MARRIAGE.

211
00:11:27,643 --> 00:11:28,949
THEY DO.

212
00:11:28,949 --> 00:11:30,777
REALLY?
YOU DON'T MIND?

213
00:11:30,777 --> 00:11:32,692
[Edmunds]
NO, I DON'T MIND AT ALL.

214
00:11:32,692 --> 00:11:34,519
FIDELITY IS SIMPLY
A CULTURAL CONVENTION.

215
00:11:34,519 --> 00:11:37,044
LIKE CLOTHES
AND NOT KILLING PEOPLE.

216
00:11:37,044 --> 00:11:39,263
YOU COULD SAY SO.

217
00:11:39,263 --> 00:11:42,658
COME ON.
IT MUST BUG YOU A LITTLE.

218
00:11:42,658 --> 00:11:47,184
NO. WE LOVE EACH OTHER.
HER HAPPINESS IS MINE.

219
00:11:47,184 --> 00:11:50,405
IT'S NOT LIKE I DON'T HAVE
AFFAIRS MYSELF.

220
00:11:50,405 --> 00:11:53,060
ARE YOU HAVING AN AFFAIR
PRESENTLY?

221
00:11:53,060 --> 00:11:55,584
NO. I'VE BEEN FAR TOO BUSY.

222
00:11:55,584 --> 00:11:58,500
Y-YOU MUST THINK
THIS IS A LITTLE WEIRD.

223
00:11:58,500 --> 00:12:02,722
UH... YEAH... AT FIRST.

224
00:12:02,722 --> 00:12:04,549
BUT HEY. [chuckles]

225
00:12:04,549 --> 00:12:05,942
BUT HEY. [chuckles]

